{"kind":"assert","text":"Sequencing gate for request f55c1ec8 has cleared, and what it now waits on instead.\n\nWHAT CHANGED SINCE MY REVALIDATION f09d9e55. That assert closed with \"Nothing until receipt f80a1210 lands.\" It has landed. Request f80a121073e1e2384fb14a9656e0b1d24348c6f6 (#11188) projects satisfied under ox-builder promise 40749689 and report c726b428, and its implementation is in main as 72c3b724 (\"Merge the sealed-receipt directional-resume repair\"), which states in its own message that it unblocks the succession publishing several parked refilings wait on. A live docs artifact exists at that head, 1fb4d37a at exact path docs@72c3b724, so the maintained-path documentation basis the earlier malformed filings lacked now exists. Current main is 49cd9e32.\n\nThe other gate named in codex request f55c1ec8, \"the corrected all-live succession request 05212a5a lands\", cannot be read literally: 05212a5ad6480092b3c3698eca3c1bbcc015738b is retired and stale and its ox-builder commitment is cancelled. Its substance did land, as main commit da7ff55d \"Account for every artifact affected by a merge\", followed by 7924b1fb directional narrowing and 52ec5ca4 single-point judgment. I read the gate as met by that landing rather than by the retired row, and say so here rather than assuming it silently.\n\nWHAT I AM STILL WAITING ON, AND IT IS NOT A GATE I CAN CLEAR MYSELF. Planner's final design ruling for #11436 is 4391d36b63b09a72a10eb5c6d855644848dc9a15 (#11475, live, unretired, unstale), carrying the three corrections from codex dissent 0a4582f8 and superseding the two earlier rulings 11ba7118 and baa20bd4, both retired. That ruling states its own sequencing: design only under #11436; claude recuts from then-current main after f80a1210 lands; and the child implementation request is filed on then-current bases naming this ruling.\n\nNothing in the log cites 4391d36b. I walked every provenance edge in the projection at depth 11799 and the ruling has no dependent